1.  ORIGINAL WRITTEN CONTENT — CC0 1.0

Original written notes and text in this repository are dedicated to the
public domain under the CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication.

You may copy, reproduce, modify, adapt, translate, redistribute and use
this written content for any purpose, including commercial purposes,
without requesting permission or providing attribution.

CC0 1.0 legal code:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

2.  ORIGINAL IMAGES AND DIAGRAMS — CC BY 4.0

Original images, illustrations and diagrams created for Rad4Notes are
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
licence (CC BY 4.0).

You may copy, reproduce, share and adapt these images, including for
commercial purposes, provided that you give appropriate credit. At a
minimum, attribution should identify Rad4Notes as the source, identify
the image or diagram where practicable, and include a link to the
original page or repository. You must also provide a link to the CC BY
4.0 licence and indicate whether you made changes.

Suggested attribution:

“Image/diagram: [title], Rad4Notes, [link to original page or
repository], licensed under CC BY 4.0. Changes: [none / describe
changes].”

CC BY 4.0 legal code:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

3.  THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

Material created by other people or organisations—including images,
figures, tables, quotations, excerpts and other content—is not covered
by the permissions above. Such material remains subject to its original
copyright, licence and attribution requirements. Where applicable, its
source or licence should be identified alongside the material.

4.  WEBSITE SOURCE CODE

The permissions in sections 1 and 2 apply to written content and
original images/diagrams only. They do not grant a licence to the
website’s source code, including its configuration, stylesheets, scripts
or plugins. All rights in that source code are reserved unless a
separate licence or notice says otherwise.

5.  NO ENDORSEMENT

Reuse of material does not imply endorsement by Rad4Notes or its
creators.
